//! RED: rem_pi on large arguments with heavy cancellation in x - k*2pi must return the correctly
//! rounded p-bit value (rm honoured; None truncates at rp(p, 64)) on every target, and the result
//! mantissa must be at most rp(p, 64) bits long. `ExactNum ==` compares by value (ext.rs
//! `impl PartialEq` uses `compare`), so the mantissa length is checked separately.
//!
//! Reference: scripts/gen_rem_pi_stress_ref.py, env mpmath-1.3.0 (mpmath 1.3.0, Python 3.12.14),
//! mp.prec = 4096. Formula rem_pi(x) = x - floor(x / 2pi) * 2pi for x > 0 (pi: OEIS A000796).
//! Inputs: 2^100; 6381956970095103 * 2^797 (J.-M. Muller, Elementary Functions, 3rd ed., Ch. 11,
//! worst case for double-precision argument reduction); round(2pi * 10^k), k = 6, 12, 18.
//! Generator output SHA256: 87dd23782d67ec001ea5effffcce0d5060d08cf9d536aa4369a1bd10a0838265

